  "note": "Ten candidates were nominated for the nine seats; four minutes before withdrawals closed at 3 p.m. on Thursday 5 May, John Rice withdrew, leaving no contest. Bernard Woods, vice-chairman, did not seek re-election. Polling day for the urban councils was Wednesday 18 May 1949 (Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1949, p. 5: \"Polling took place yesterday for the election of county borough, borough and urban councils in Ulster\")."
